.TH TUI_CMDLINE_INIT 3 2026-11-11 "libtuikit 1.1" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_cmdline_init, tui_cmdline_free, tui_cmdline_register, tui_cmdline_count,
tui_cmdline_name, tui_cmdline_help, tui_cmdline_handle, tui_cmdline_is_open,
tui_cmdline_message, tui_cmdline_render \- the command line opened by ':'
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/cmdline.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef int (*tui_cmdline_fn)(void *" user ", const char *" args ,
.BI "                             char *" msg ", size_t " size );
.PP
.BI "void tui_cmdline_init(tui_cmdline *" cl );
.BI "void tui_cmdline_free(tui_cmdline *" cl );
.BI "int  tui_cmdline_register(tui_cmdline *" cl ", const char *" name ,
.BI "                         const char *" help ", tui_cmdline_fn " fn ", void *" user );
.BI "int  tui_cmdline_count(const tui_cmdline *" cl );
.BI "const char *tui_cmdline_name(const tui_cmdline *" cl ", int " i );
.BI "const char *tui_cmdline_help(const tui_cmdline *" cl ", int " i );
.BI "tui_cmdline_result tui_cmdline_handle(tui_cmdline *" cl ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "int  tui_cmdline_is_open(const tui_cmdline *" cl );
.BI "const char *tui_cmdline_message(const tui_cmdline *" cl ", int *" ok );
.BI "void tui_cmdline_render(tui_cmdline *" cl ", tui_canvas " c );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The vim-like command line of policies/tui-interface-model.md: one input line at
the bottom of the screen, opened by
.BR : .
(The action menu is on
.BR \- ;
see
.BR tui_keytable_init (3).)
.PP
A program registers its commands with
.BR tui_cmdline_register ():
a name (one word), a help text and a handler.
Registering a name again replaces it.
The handler gets the text after the name in
.I args
and writes the message to show into
.IR msg ;
it returns 0 for success (the message is drawn in the ok role) or non-zero
(the error role).
With no command registered
.B :
is unbound:
.BR tui_cmdline_handle ()
returns
.BR TUI_CMDLINE_IGNORED .
.PP
.BR tui_cmdline_handle ()
gives every event to the line.
While it is closed only a plain
.B :
does anything: it opens the line and returns
.BR TUI_CMDLINE_EDITING .
While it is open it takes every event (the program must not use one):
Esc, Ctrl-C, Ctrl-D and Backspace on an empty line cancel
.RB ( TUI_CMDLINE_CANCELLED );
Enter runs the command
.RB ( TUI_CMDLINE_RAN ;
an unknown name leaves the message
"unknown command: NAME" as an error);
Up and Down browse the lines run before; the other keys edit as in
.BR tui_lineedit_init (3).
Tab completes the command name (the first word) to the longest prefix the
matching commands share; a lone match gets a blank after it, several are
listed on the row above the line.
.PP
.BR tui_cmdline_render ()
draws the last row of
.IR c :
":" and the text with the terminal cursor while the line is open, else the
message of the last command until the line is opened again.
.BR tui_cmdline_message ()
returns it ("" when there is none) and in
.I ok
whether it succeeded.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR tui_cmdline_register ()
returns 0, or \-1 with errno EINVAL (no name, a name with a blank, no handler)
or ENOMEM.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_lineedit_init (3),
.BR tui_keytable_init (3),
.BR libtuikit (7)
